  "report": {
    "question": "How does the CUBIC congestion control algorithm in TCP differ from Reno?",
    "content": "The main difference between TCP Reno and TCP Cubic is the window increase function. While Reno uses the traditional linear increase (W=W+1), Cubic implements a binary search increase which can reach the available bandwidth much faster than Reno. Earlier TCP congestion control algorithms such as Reno and New Reno rely on linear growth of the congestion window (cwnd). Instead, the window size is a cubic function of the time since the last congestion event.",
